use Libraries.Web.Page.QuorumPage

/*
    The EPIQ Event Details page (plan 13 phase 5B): its title (the old page
    had none), the header picture, pictures beside words, questions that
    open (the old accordion), and the contact tiles.
*/
class EpiqEvent is QuorumPage
    on create
        SetLocation("eventEpiq.html")
        SetShortTitle("Computer Science Professional Development in Quorum")
        SetDescription("Join an EPIQ community of people learning the Quorum programming language at our annual conference: Experience Programming in Quorum.")
    end

    action Setup
        SetWebPageTitle("Experience Programming in Quorum (EPIQ) - Quorum Programming Language")
        Title("EPIQ Event Details")
        Image("media/userInterface/quorumAssets/epiq-banner-3.png", "Professionals posing in front of Washington School for the Blind")
        Section("What is EPIQ?")
        PictureBeside("media/userInterface/quorumAssets/social.png", "Two bunnies interacting with each other", "The Experience Programming in Quorum (EPIQ) event is a computer programming training workshop designed largely for K-12 teachers. We help teachers learn how to invent anything from code with robotics, to computer graphics or games, or any number of things.")
        PictureBesideLink("EPIQ Schedule", "https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1oA0f0GU5_8Y7RHT8ZSTGb4Cl1FFxCtdFu8GmEMRTjY8/edit")
        Section("Where is EPIQ hosted?")
        PictureBeside("media/userInterface/quorumAssets/comingSoon.png", "Quincy climing to his goals", "For EPIQ 2026, we will be at the University of Nevada, Las Vegas in Las Vegas, NV. Dates are June 22nd - June 26th, 2026.")
        Section("Before you arrive")
        PictureBeside("media/userInterface/quorumAssets/arrival.png", "Quincy on his laptop thinking about Quorum", "Depending on the year, there is typically an application to attend the venue, depending on if you are requesting funding or part of a program. These materials are not yet available for the 2025 year.")
        Section("Frequently Asked Questions")
        Paragraph("Please contact us at contact@qorf.org for any other additional details or assistance")
        Question("What operating systems are supported?", "We recommend either a Mac or PC. In the case of using a PC, Windows 10 or above is required. For Mac, we recommend using the latest operating system.")
        Question("What technical specifications does the machine need to have?", "In both cases, what kind of machine you need to run depends partially on what you want to invent. If you are creating small little text programs, then you do not need much. But, if you are creating games, especially, they can require a decent graphics chip and quite a bit of memory. It is typical at the event to recommend at least 16 gigs of ram and on Mac and an M1 or higher processor. However, it can run on 8 gigs with an Intel chip. For PC, we again recommend 16 gigs of memory, but 8 will do and most modern processors will be sufficient.")
        Question("What kind of accessibility support is there?", "Generally, all of the technologies we make are accessible, but at the bleeding edge. What we mean is that we follow as many of the modern standards for accessibility as we can, but sometimes what we invent does not have an accompanying standard. For example, 3D games do not have an associated accessibility standard, or at least not really on a technical level, so we have guessed as best as we can. We make changes every release based on feedback in collaboration with people with disabilities.")
        Question("How much programming experience do I need to participate?", "None. Many people that come to EPIQ have never programmed before. There is always a cohort, however, of people that come back year on year to try all the new stuff. Everyone will get a mix of new and old stuff and we plan carefully for that.")
        Question("I'm terrified of learning to code. Help?", "Coding takes practice, but honestly it is pretty rare to come to EPIQ and not feel like you have made progress. You get 5 days of practicing with a friendly community making games, coding robots, or other fun stuff. Just like any area of science, there are lots of little tricks and we start from the beginning.")
        Section("Talk to Us")
        Paragraph("Stay up to date and join the network of Quorum professionals!")
        Choices()
        Choice("Discord", "https://discord.gg/6yTVQq4", "media/userInterface/SVG/choice-discord.svg")
        Choice("Email List", "https://groups.google.com/g/quorum-language", "media/userInterface/SVG/choice-mail.svg")
        Choice("Help", "/bugs.html", "media/userInterface/SVG/choice-help.svg")
    end
end
